Usage: benchmark run [-hV] [--debug] [--nsys] [--gpu-sanitizer
                     [=<gpuSanitizer>]] [--concurrency=<concurrency>]
                     [--data=<dataLocation>]
                     [--external-profiler-go-file=<externalProfilerGoFile>]
                     [--external-profiler-ready-file=<externalProfilerReadyFile>
                     ]
                     [--external-profiler-timeout-seconds=<externalProfilerTimeo
                     utSeconds>] [--fs-cache=<fsCacheDirectory>] [-m=<mode>]
                     [-p=<profileEvent>] [-r=<runs>] [-w=<warmup>]
                     [-W=<suiteWarmup>] [-q=<queries>]... [-s=<skipQueries>]...
Run benchmark queries with optional profiling and result validation.
      --concurrency=<concurrency>
                          Maximum number of queries to execute simultaneously.
                            All --runs queries are submitted at once; each
                            measures its own elapsed time independently.
                            Default: 1. Incompatible with --gpu-memory-trace.
      --data=<dataLocation>
                          Data directory or URI (e.g. s3://bucket/prefix).
                            Default: workload-specific.
      --debug             Enable debug logging
      --external-profiler-go-file=<externalProfilerGoFile>
                          Signal file allowing measurements to begin after an
                            external profiler attaches
      --external-profiler-ready-file=<externalProfilerReadyFile>
                          After suite warmup, write the benchmark JVM PID to
                            this file and wait for --external-profiler-go-file
      --external-profiler-timeout-seconds=<externalProfilerTimeoutSeconds>
                          Maximum wait for the external profiler signal.
                            Default: 60
      --fs-cache=<fsCacheDirectory>
                          Directory backing an OS-local filesystem cache for
                            remote reads. When set, the workload enables fs.
                            cache.* against this directory; reads are uncached
                            when unset.
      --gpu-sanitizer[=<gpuSanitizer>]
                          Run the benchmark JVM under NVIDIA compute-sanitizer
                            with the given arguments (e.g. "--tool memcheck
                            --leak-check full"). Defaults to "--tool memcheck"
                            when passed with no value. Requires --mode=gpu.
  -h, --help              Show this help message and exit.
  -m, --mode=<mode>       Execution backend: CPU, NITRO, GPU. Default: CPU.
      --nsys              Run the benchmark JVM under nsys profile. Optional
                            value is extra nsys arguments. Requires --mode=gpu.
  -p, --profile=<profileEvent>
                          async-profiler event: NONE, CPU, WALL. Default: NONE.
  -q, --query=<queries>   A specific query number to run (can be repeated)
  -r, --runs=<runs>       Number of measured runs for each query
  -s, --skip-query=<skipQueries>
                          A query number to skip; recorded as all-zero timings
                            in the CSV (can be repeated)
  -V, --version           Print version information and exit.
  -w, --warmup=<warmup>   Number of warmup runs for each query
  -W, --suite-warmup=<suiteWarmup>
                          Number of full passes over the workload's default
                            queries (in order, no validation) before per-query
                            benchmarking. Always runs the entire workload —
                            independent of --query.
